# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source corpora — never commit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The README states that this repository reproduces no substantial portion of
# any source text. One careless `git add -A` would falsify that. Source
# material — including the Plutarch-Thoughts checkout the locators point into —
# stays on the machine that runs the distillation.
corpus/
corpora/
content/
Plutarch-Thoughts/
*.pdf
*.epub
*.mobi
*.azw
*.azw3
*.docx
*.doc
*.rtf
*.odt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Distillation run artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The pipeline's work directory and the intermediate artifacts it writes.
# These are reproducible from the corpus and are not repository content.
persona_work/
.persona_work/
work/
boundaries.json
coverage_map.json
extractions.json
scores.json
fidelity.json
manifest.json
passages.json
split.json

# Nested persona outputs, if this package is ever used to generate another.
*-perspective/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python — the boundary-detection and metrics scripts are stdlib-only, but a
# contributor may still create these locally.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

